1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,940
Yes, Ginko committed a grave crime ground.

2
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:11,940
Ginko is the reason why Tsubikai's dead!

3
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:16,120
How could you, Ginko?

4
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,700
I'll never forgive you, bears!

5
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:21,040
I'll ruin you now!

6
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:21,980
Everyone!

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,740
From the beginning, we hated you.

8
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:44,760
But also, we loved you from the beginning as well.

9
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:48,760
All we wanted was to become true friends with you.

10
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:52,280
So, we had to cross the wall.

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:54,800
Kirikuma!

12
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:58,180
Ahhhhhhhhhhh!

13
00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:00,560
Kirikuma Orochi!

14
00:02:33,027 --> 00:02:36,027
Girls, this is, like, way bad.

15
00:02:36,027 --> 00:02:39,027
People are saying another bear was here yesterday.

16
00:02:39,027 --> 00:02:42,027
Yeah, but I heard it was exterminated immediately.

17
00:02:42,027 --> 00:02:44,027
That same girl shot it, right?

18
00:02:44,027 --> 00:02:46,027
The one the Invisible Storm isn't a huge fan of?

19
00:02:46,027 --> 00:02:48,027
Yeah, but... and don't tell anyone,

20
00:02:48,027 --> 00:02:50,027
because it's, like, way secret.

21
00:02:50,027 --> 00:02:53,027
Apparently that bear is, like, way still alive.

22
00:03:02,027 --> 00:03:04,027
That's all right, oh!

23
00:03:04,027 --> 00:03:26,147
I

24
00:03:26,147 --> 00:03:33,767
Welcome to the Door to Friendship, Ginko.

25
00:03:33,767 --> 00:03:35,067
You silly girl.

26
00:03:47,347 --> 00:03:49,987
I've finally gotten rid of the nuisance.

27
00:03:50,967 --> 00:03:52,127
Ginko, you're a shiro.

28
00:03:52,127 --> 00:03:56,847
You were the girl Reya gave her pendant to on that stormy night so long ago.

29
00:03:57,927 --> 00:04:00,007
And what a stupid girl you were.

30
00:04:01,787 --> 00:04:04,667
Instead of getting love, you fell into the abyss.

31
00:04:05,347 --> 00:04:07,027
It's all your own fault, dear.

32
00:04:07,547 --> 00:04:11,307
You knew Lulu Yurigasaki loved you, but you pretended not to see.

33
00:04:12,007 --> 00:04:14,107
And then you tried to abandon her.

34
00:04:14,607 --> 00:04:16,947
Now you're paying the price for that sin.

35
00:04:18,347 --> 00:04:19,587
Guess what, Reya?

36
00:04:19,587 --> 00:04:24,607
Reya, your sweet girl, the precious daughter you loved so much is almost mine.

37
00:04:25,647 --> 00:04:27,787
And now I'll make her my bride in the box.

38
00:04:28,487 --> 00:04:29,707
Yes, today.

39
00:04:34,247 --> 00:04:37,087
I'm going to eat Kureha Tsubaki.

40
00:04:37,587 --> 00:04:38,027
Kuro!

41
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:48,787
I lost it.

42
00:04:49,567 --> 00:04:51,587
You should be thankful you're alive.

43
00:04:51,827 --> 00:04:52,887
For now, at least.

44
00:04:55,707 --> 00:04:57,707
Goodness, did I surprise you?

45
00:04:58,007 --> 00:04:58,987
Why are you here?

46
00:04:59,247 --> 00:05:00,427
I thought you were dead.

47
00:05:00,687 --> 00:05:01,207
Grow, grow.

48
00:05:01,727 --> 00:05:04,087
Well, you thought right because I am dead.

49
00:05:04,087 --> 00:05:07,087
It's crazy, but you're the only one who can see me right now.

50
00:05:09,407 --> 00:05:10,427
Everything's fine.

51
00:05:10,967 --> 00:05:15,787
Just think of me as a ghost named Desire that happens to dwell inside you right here.

52
00:05:17,247 --> 00:05:19,127
Is that explanation enough?

53
00:05:20,027 --> 00:05:21,107
Where are we?

54
00:05:21,327 --> 00:05:22,467
The door to friendship.

55
00:05:23,327 --> 00:05:27,287
The center of the sky that divides the worlds of moon and forest.

56
00:05:27,287 --> 00:05:30,267
This is the place where true love is tested.

57
00:05:31,747 --> 00:05:33,467
Now tell me something, Ginko.

58
00:05:33,847 --> 00:05:37,467
I'm dying to hear how you were the one who killed Sumika Izumino.

59
00:05:40,147 --> 00:05:42,947
I say early tomorrow morning, we come back here.

60
00:05:43,307 --> 00:05:44,927
Then the flower bed can get fixed.

61
00:05:45,307 --> 00:05:46,727
I don't mind helping you at all.

62
00:05:47,867 --> 00:05:48,687
Thanks, Mitsuko.

63
00:05:48,807 --> 00:05:50,047
That's so generous of you.

64
00:05:50,287 --> 00:05:50,707
Great.

65
00:05:50,887 --> 00:05:51,667
We're both in.

66
00:05:51,707 --> 00:05:52,987
Are you meeting us too, Kureha?

67
00:05:53,187 --> 00:05:53,987
Oh, yeah.

68
00:05:53,987 --> 00:05:54,287
Huh?

69
00:05:54,287 --> 00:05:54,347
Huh?

70
00:05:54,347 --> 00:05:59,047
Who did that?

71
00:06:02,307 --> 00:06:04,567
I sensed something was wrong then.

72
00:06:07,447 --> 00:06:11,527
I had a rival at the school who was also after my Kureha Tsubaki.

73
00:06:12,027 --> 00:06:14,407
A bear in human form other than me.

74
00:06:14,847 --> 00:06:15,687
Well, me and Konami.

75
00:06:16,207 --> 00:06:20,307
If I didn't hurry and make my move, another bear was going to get to her before I could.

76
00:06:20,767 --> 00:06:21,247
So.

77
00:06:24,347 --> 00:06:25,387
Bye.

78
00:06:25,627 --> 00:06:26,727
I'm headed this way.

79
00:06:27,067 --> 00:06:28,047
See you in the morning.

80
00:06:30,887 --> 00:06:31,847
Listen, Sumika.

81
00:06:32,067 --> 00:06:33,647
I have an idea about tomorrow.

82
00:06:34,567 --> 00:06:36,547
Why don't we arrange a surprise for Kureha?

83
00:06:36,847 --> 00:06:37,447
A surprise?

84
00:06:38,227 --> 00:06:41,427
I know someone with lilies in bloom who would probably give us some.

85
00:06:41,587 --> 00:06:42,867
Don't you think she'd love that?

86
00:06:43,447 --> 00:06:45,947
I can pick them up tonight so we can plant them for her.

87
00:06:46,247 --> 00:06:46,727
Really?

88
00:06:47,427 --> 00:06:47,807
Yeah.

89
00:06:48,327 --> 00:06:49,187
It'll be great.

90
00:06:49,527 --> 00:06:51,307
So tomorrow morning, meet me there early.

91
00:06:51,587 --> 00:06:55,127
And together, we'll fill the flower bed full of lilies before she arrives.

92
00:06:55,727 --> 00:06:56,127
Okay.

93
00:06:56,727 --> 00:06:57,887
But what if she...

94
00:06:57,887 --> 00:07:00,007
I bet it will make Kureha so happy.

95
00:07:00,207 --> 00:07:02,287
It'll be just like a magic fairy visited.

96
00:07:02,287 --> 00:07:08,407
It's funny.

97
00:07:08,807 --> 00:07:10,467
That girl would have done anything I said.

98
00:07:10,767 --> 00:07:12,927
All I had to do was mention it was for Kureha.

99
00:07:14,127 --> 00:07:15,207
Now come on.

100
00:07:15,427 --> 00:07:17,047
Be honest with me, won't you?

101
00:07:17,047 --> 00:07:27,367
The truth is, you found out that I was targeting Sumika Izumina, didn't you?

102
00:07:33,367 --> 00:07:35,347
You should learn how to hide better.

103
00:07:35,907 --> 00:07:37,607
I knew all along you were there.

104
00:07:38,247 --> 00:07:40,807
Following Sumika to see what made her so great.

105
00:07:43,807 --> 00:07:44,967
Will you get some?

106
00:07:45,167 --> 00:07:46,247
They are very lovely.

107
00:07:46,247 --> 00:07:46,727
What?

108
00:07:47,447 --> 00:07:49,647
Oh, you're one of the new transfer students.

109
00:07:49,747 --> 00:07:50,007
Hi.

110
00:07:53,387 --> 00:07:54,267
Sniff, sniff.

111
00:07:56,167 --> 00:07:57,567
They smell amazing.

112
00:07:58,327 --> 00:08:00,467
I'm guessing you must be a fan of lilies, too.

113
00:08:01,047 --> 00:08:02,047
I adore them.

114
00:08:02,467 --> 00:08:03,127
They're lovely.

115
00:08:03,547 --> 00:08:05,287
And they make me think of a special memory.

116
00:08:07,047 --> 00:08:08,907
A special memory with a friend.

117
00:08:09,167 --> 00:08:10,567
A friend I happen to love.

118
00:08:13,147 --> 00:08:15,227
I won't back down on that love.

119
00:08:16,247 --> 00:08:20,607
Because the love my friend gave me can't be taken away by anyone.

120
00:08:20,607 --> 00:08:25,227
Oh, I'm sorry.

121
00:08:25,707 --> 00:08:29,067
I bet it was weird for me to say something like that when we've only just met.

122
00:08:29,067 --> 00:08:32,467
Yeah, you were jealous of her, weren't you?

123
00:08:32,467 --> 00:08:39,267
The love you dreamed about and wanted so badly from Kareha had already been given to another girl.

124
00:08:39,267 --> 00:08:48,887
And yet, you still wanted to see her again.

125
00:08:48,887 --> 00:08:53,167
In fact, this time, you didn't even tell your partner what you were up to.

126
00:08:54,287 --> 00:08:55,067
Why go?

127
00:08:55,427 --> 00:08:57,287
Did you plan to warn her about me?

128
00:08:57,647 --> 00:08:58,047
Yes.

129
00:08:58,587 --> 00:08:59,547
That was the idea.

130
00:08:59,547 --> 00:09:04,707
Oh, stupid me.

131
00:09:04,707 --> 00:09:07,207
How could I go and lose the hairpin again?

132
00:09:07,627 --> 00:09:07,947
Here.

133
00:09:12,827 --> 00:09:13,347
Ginko!

134
00:09:13,607 --> 00:09:14,767
You found it!

135
00:09:14,867 --> 00:09:15,447
Thank you!

136
00:09:15,947 --> 00:09:16,887
What a relief.

137
00:09:17,347 --> 00:09:18,207
I'm so silly.

138
00:09:18,647 --> 00:09:21,127
This is the second time someone's found this pin for me.

139
00:09:21,727 --> 00:09:24,107
I lost it the day of the entrance ceremony, too.

140
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:26,307
The friend I told you about yesterday?

141
00:09:26,567 --> 00:09:27,967
She's the one who found it before.

142
00:09:28,107 --> 00:09:28,707
Neat, huh?

143
00:09:29,307 --> 00:09:31,447
She found it for you before?

144
00:09:32,187 --> 00:09:32,667
Yep.

145
00:09:33,327 --> 00:09:35,587
This hairpin has brought me friendship and love.

146
00:09:36,307 --> 00:09:38,367
I like to think of it as my special charm.

147
00:09:38,987 --> 00:09:39,687
Thank you.

148
00:09:39,847 --> 00:09:41,167
It means so much to me.

149
00:09:41,647 --> 00:09:43,847
I really, really appreciate it, Ginko.

150
00:09:44,247 --> 00:09:46,847
Now I'd better hurry up and run or I'll be late.

151
00:09:47,847 --> 00:09:48,327
Where?

152
00:09:48,327 --> 00:09:55,247
I was first, though.

153
00:09:56,007 --> 00:09:57,387
She found me first.

154
00:09:57,927 --> 00:09:58,727
Growl, growl.

155
00:10:00,547 --> 00:10:01,567
That's right.

156
00:10:02,067 --> 00:10:06,267
If you had gone ahead and stopped her then, Sumika Izumino wouldn't have had to die.

157
00:10:06,987 --> 00:10:10,467
Koreha Tsubaki wouldn't have had to lose her very best friend, either.

158
00:10:11,467 --> 00:10:12,287
I know.

159
00:10:13,427 --> 00:10:14,747
I couldn't help it.

160
00:10:15,787 --> 00:10:17,007
Sumika was in my way.

161
00:10:17,007 --> 00:10:21,767
And we exclude those in our way.

162
00:10:22,187 --> 00:10:25,387
It would be so much easier if we were just honest about what we want.

163
00:10:26,527 --> 00:10:28,127
So that's the truth.

164
00:10:28,627 --> 00:10:29,487
I'm guilty.

165
00:10:30,747 --> 00:10:32,507
I wanted Sumika to die.

166
00:10:35,507 --> 00:10:37,367
Well, good morning, Sumika.

167
00:10:42,687 --> 00:10:44,907
Such a lovely morning.

168
00:10:44,907 --> 00:10:46,907
And I'm practically starving.

169
00:10:47,967 --> 00:10:51,127
You witnessed me attacking sweet little Sumika.

170
00:10:51,547 --> 00:10:53,427
And you just sat there and watched.

171
00:10:53,967 --> 00:10:55,467
You allowed her to die.

172
00:10:56,067 --> 00:10:57,547
You could have saved her.

173
00:10:58,027 --> 00:10:58,847
But you didn't.

174
00:11:00,047 --> 00:11:02,187
Technically, yes, I'm the one who ate her.

175
00:11:02,707 --> 00:11:04,947
But who was the one that really killed her?

176
00:11:06,347 --> 00:11:07,467
It was me.

177
00:11:07,467 --> 00:11:08,507
Indeed it was.

178
00:11:08,507 --> 00:11:09,107
Indeed it was.

179
00:11:09,107 --> 00:11:11,767
In that moment, you were a slave of desire.

180
00:11:12,647 --> 00:11:15,707
Jealousy got a hold of you and drove you to a terrible crime.

181
00:11:16,007 --> 00:11:17,127
I'm a criminal there.

182
00:11:17,467 --> 00:11:18,027
Grow, grow.

183
00:11:18,527 --> 00:11:19,027
Yes.

184
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:23,367
However, is there really any creature that doesn't sin in order to live?

185
00:11:23,367 --> 00:11:26,487
Koreha Tsubaki forgot you.

186
00:11:26,827 --> 00:11:27,527
Her friend.

187
00:11:27,907 --> 00:11:30,167
And then she gave her love to Sumika instead.

188
00:11:31,167 --> 00:11:32,747
Now, pay attention.

189
00:11:33,207 --> 00:11:35,047
Only one thing in this world is certain.

190
00:11:35,167 --> 00:11:37,867
And believe you me, it's not friendship or love.

191
00:11:37,867 --> 00:11:42,727
Desire is the only thing you can count on, dear Ginkgo.

192
00:11:43,267 --> 00:11:44,887
Love is a savage emotion.

193
00:11:45,847 --> 00:11:47,687
To love another is to rule them.

194
00:11:48,667 --> 00:11:52,907
To want to become one with them so badly you consume them is truly cruel.

195
00:11:52,907 --> 00:11:56,507
I know something else you might want to hear, shall I tell you.

196
00:11:57,187 --> 00:11:59,747
There's another bear at that school besides us.

197
00:12:00,527 --> 00:12:02,287
A very cunning bear at that.

198
00:12:02,867 --> 00:12:04,547
She got Koreha to kill me.

199
00:12:04,847 --> 00:12:07,607
And she got Lulu Yurigasaki to betray you.

200
00:12:08,547 --> 00:12:13,207
I hate to admit it, but that bitch bear had all of us dancing to her own little tune.

201
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:17,807
Everything she's done is because she's after Koreha.

202
00:12:17,807 --> 00:12:23,247
If you don't hurry and stop her, you'll lose Koreha forever this time.

203
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:30,507
Are you ready to become one with me, Ginkgo?

204
00:12:30,887 --> 00:12:33,587
The time has come to prove your love.

205
00:12:33,587 --> 00:12:48,947
Grow, grow, grow, grow, grow!

206
00:12:48,947 --> 00:12:49,287
Grow!

207
00:12:53,287 --> 00:13:02,247
I'm going to eat her.

208
00:13:02,247 --> 00:13:04,807
I have to grow, grow, grow, grow.

209
00:13:21,187 --> 00:13:24,967
These photos were totally discovered in the locker of Kaoru Harishima,

210
00:13:25,127 --> 00:13:27,807
who recently, like, way died in a bear attack.

211
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:35,507
Konami Yurikawa, as you can see, was actually a bear disguised as a human girl.

212
00:13:39,627 --> 00:13:41,467
This is scary, like, way.

213
00:13:41,787 --> 00:13:44,147
Bears got across the wall pretending to be human.

214
00:13:44,467 --> 00:13:47,207
And they've, like, way eaten our friends one after the other.

215
00:13:50,207 --> 00:13:52,987
We all see what this like means, don't we?

216
00:13:52,987 --> 00:13:57,127
That's right, there's, like, a bear in this class.

217
00:13:57,427 --> 00:13:59,647
A bear hiding among us, like, for real.

218
00:14:01,787 --> 00:14:03,927
Bears, like, way stick out from our crowd.

219
00:14:04,427 --> 00:14:06,467
Bears refuse to, like, fit in with us.

220
00:14:06,967 --> 00:14:09,507
Bears are evil and can't follow social cues.

221
00:14:11,667 --> 00:14:12,607
Here we go.

222
00:14:12,767 --> 00:14:13,927
They've started up again.

223
00:14:14,727 --> 00:14:15,087
Yep.

224
00:14:15,087 --> 00:14:18,567
But, Kureha Tsubaki is attending the meeting this time.

225
00:14:19,307 --> 00:14:21,347
They made her a friend at this late date?

226
00:14:21,807 --> 00:14:23,027
Very interesting.

227
00:14:23,587 --> 00:14:25,327
Have they canceled her exclusion then?

228
00:14:25,707 --> 00:14:27,147
Ah, who can tell?

229
00:14:28,287 --> 00:14:31,527
Those girls are always looking for some evil to exclude.

230
00:14:32,187 --> 00:14:36,527
Doesn't matter to them whether the evil is a person or a bear or even really evil.

231
00:14:37,327 --> 00:14:40,047
The ritual of banding together to exclude someone

232
00:14:40,047 --> 00:14:43,067
is what makes the invisible connection they like to call us

233
00:14:43,067 --> 00:14:44,587
feel as if it's real to them.

234
00:14:46,207 --> 00:14:48,087
It looks like they're almost there.

235
00:14:48,527 --> 00:14:49,507
For that is sexy.

236
00:14:50,187 --> 00:14:51,467
Shabbat-dod-do.

237
00:14:54,207 --> 00:14:56,307
Shall I put in another coin?

238
00:14:56,947 --> 00:14:57,307
Yeah.

239
00:14:58,427 --> 00:14:59,947
Shabbat-dod-do.

240
00:15:01,547 --> 00:15:04,047
Let us now begin the exclusion ceremony.

241
00:15:06,047 --> 00:15:09,567
Please name whom we think the bear lurking among us is.

242
00:15:10,047 --> 00:15:12,467
Let's search bear!

243
00:15:40,047 --> 00:15:50,267
People who like shelter bears are accomplices!

244
00:15:55,667 --> 00:15:56,727
Tell me, Mom.

245
00:15:57,547 --> 00:15:58,047
Did I...

246
00:15:58,867 --> 00:16:00,967
Did I do the right thing that day?

247
00:16:04,667 --> 00:16:05,147
Lulu.

248
00:16:05,147 --> 00:16:08,767
Curry pie, Lulu knows the truth.

249
00:16:09,067 --> 00:16:10,907
She found out what Ginko did to Sumika.

250
00:16:12,247 --> 00:16:15,127
Yes, Ginko committed a grave crime, Growl.

251
00:16:15,767 --> 00:16:17,387
Ginko is why Sumika's dead!

252
00:16:17,807 --> 00:16:19,047
She helped the killer!

253
00:16:20,727 --> 00:16:21,967
Ginko, is that true?

254
00:16:23,107 --> 00:16:25,087
Yes, it's true, Growl, Growl.

255
00:16:25,087 --> 00:16:27,767
I killed Sumika Izumino.

256
00:16:28,807 --> 00:16:29,627
It was me!

257
00:16:38,007 --> 00:16:40,267
Mitsuko Yurizono killed Sumika.

258
00:16:40,867 --> 00:16:43,007
I know that for a fact, so...

259
00:16:43,007 --> 00:16:45,547
Why would Ginko confess to it?

260
00:16:47,887 --> 00:16:49,747
What's the truth and what's a lie?

261
00:16:50,347 --> 00:16:52,487
I don't understand any of this.

262
00:16:53,187 --> 00:16:53,607
Ball.

263
00:16:54,927 --> 00:16:55,427
Ball.

264
00:16:56,767 --> 00:16:57,267
Ball.

265
00:16:58,627 --> 00:16:59,087
Ball.

266
00:17:01,927 --> 00:17:02,307
Yes?

267
00:17:04,387 --> 00:17:09,007
This call is a challenge from the Wall of Severance.

268
00:17:09,007 --> 00:17:10,547
Kureha Tsubaki.

269
00:17:11,267 --> 00:17:14,587
If your love is true, go to the Lily Bird immediately.

270
00:17:15,707 --> 00:17:17,867
The bear in question will be waiting for you.

271
00:17:18,527 --> 00:17:19,867
She's at the flower pit?

272
00:17:20,367 --> 00:17:21,507
Ginko's waiting for me?

273
00:17:21,807 --> 00:17:23,527
Give yourself over to the bears,

274
00:17:23,867 --> 00:17:25,607
and your love will be approved.

275
00:17:27,067 --> 00:17:28,867
I'm going to go talk to Ginko.

276
00:17:29,607 --> 00:17:32,347
And this time, I'm going to find out what really happened.

277
00:17:33,087 --> 00:17:33,407
Huh.

278
00:17:33,827 --> 00:17:35,747
To think she masqueraded as us

279
00:17:35,747 --> 00:17:37,807
to make a prank call to Kureha Tsubaki.

280
00:17:39,007 --> 00:17:40,807
Oh, that Yuri Ika Hakonaka.

281
00:17:41,327 --> 00:17:42,207
She is guilty.

282
00:17:42,507 --> 00:17:42,947
Mm-hmm.

283
00:17:43,387 --> 00:17:44,987
Although, what she's about to do

284
00:17:44,987 --> 00:17:47,267
is why she made the contract with us to begin with.

285
00:17:47,587 --> 00:17:50,327
So, she's probably ready for the consequences.

286
00:17:50,947 --> 00:17:51,847
Sparkle, sparkle.

287
00:17:52,307 --> 00:17:54,767
All shall be as according to Kumaria's will.

288
00:17:55,767 --> 00:17:57,027
For that is sexy.

289
00:17:58,107 --> 00:17:59,087
Shabba da do.

290
00:18:03,087 --> 00:18:03,687
Ginko.

291
00:18:04,007 --> 00:18:05,747
What happened between us?

292
00:18:06,347 --> 00:18:07,807
I want to know the truth.

293
00:18:07,807 --> 00:18:13,007
Dearest Raya,

294
00:18:13,507 --> 00:18:15,407
do you remember that stormy night?

295
00:18:17,407 --> 00:18:19,667
Do you remember the moment I ate you?

296
00:18:20,087 --> 00:18:22,507
Do you remember when I put you in the box of myself

297
00:18:22,507 --> 00:18:23,747
to fill in my gaps?

298
00:18:24,227 --> 00:18:25,547
But I wasn't fulfilled.

299
00:18:26,407 --> 00:18:28,027
I was still so empty.

300
00:18:28,027 --> 00:18:31,847
I figured out why, though.

301
00:18:32,287 --> 00:18:34,847
It was because you had given all your love away to her.

302
00:18:35,247 --> 00:18:36,767
So I decided to wait.

303
00:18:37,407 --> 00:18:38,227
Until now.

304
00:18:39,007 --> 00:18:41,847
I waited until that girl who stole your love from me

305
00:18:41,847 --> 00:18:42,967
finally grew up.

306
00:18:43,407 --> 00:18:46,347
And I waited as your love gradually and beautifully

307
00:18:46,347 --> 00:18:47,927
blossomed inside of her.

308
00:18:47,927 --> 00:18:51,927
I did all this in a blank world robbed of color.

309
00:18:52,447 --> 00:18:53,067
I waited.

310
00:18:53,427 --> 00:18:54,027
And waited.

311
00:18:54,547 --> 00:18:55,127
And waited.

312
00:18:56,127 --> 00:18:57,007
At last.

313
00:18:57,347 --> 00:18:57,687
Yes.

314
00:18:57,687 --> 00:19:02,627
The flower has bloomed.

315
00:19:03,287 --> 00:19:05,607
Today, I will eat your daughter.

316
00:19:06,247 --> 00:19:09,087
Today, I will eat Koreha Tsubaki.

317
00:19:09,087 --> 00:19:15,987
Ginko, where are you?

318
00:19:20,587 --> 00:19:21,087
It...

319
00:19:21,187 --> 00:19:22,247
It...

320
00:19:22,247 --> 00:19:22,927
It...

321
00:19:22,927 --> 00:19:25,807
It...

322
00:19:25,807 --> 00:19:28,807
This... this is wrong!

323
00:19:28,807 --> 00:19:30,807
That bear isn't Ginkgo!

324
00:19:30,807 --> 00:19:33,807
Oh, Rhea, she looks just like you.

325
00:19:33,807 --> 00:19:36,807
Her eyes, her hair...

326
00:19:36,807 --> 00:19:38,807
She even has your smell.

327
00:19:38,807 --> 00:19:42,807
Kureha Tsubaki, give your love to me!

328
00:19:44,807 --> 00:19:47,807
You and I are going to become one forever!

329
00:19:55,807 --> 00:19:59,807
Take my kiss now, Kureha, my darling.

330
00:19:59,807 --> 00:20:01,807
This kiss is a special one.

331
00:20:01,807 --> 00:20:04,807
It's for my precious bride-in-the-box.

332
00:20:11,807 --> 00:20:14,807
That was like a way super close call.

333
00:20:14,807 --> 00:20:16,807
Choco? Oh...

334
00:20:16,807 --> 00:20:18,807
The bear ran away! After it!

335
00:20:20,807 --> 00:20:22,807
Wait, that's...

336
00:20:25,807 --> 00:20:29,807
Eureka!

337
00:20:29,807 --> 00:20:30,807
Eureka!

338
00:20:30,807 --> 00:20:31,807
Eureka!

339
00:20:31,807 --> 00:20:32,807
Eureka!

340
00:20:32,807 --> 00:20:33,807
Eureka!

341
00:20:33,807 --> 00:20:34,807
Eureka!

342
00:20:34,807 --> 00:20:35,807
Eureka!

343
00:20:35,807 --> 00:20:36,807
Eureka!

344
00:20:37,807 --> 00:20:40,807
Rhea, you found me again.

345
00:20:42,807 --> 00:20:44,807
I missed you so much.

346
00:20:44,807 --> 00:20:48,807
Oh, how I've longed to see you just one more time, and here you are.

347
00:20:48,807 --> 00:20:51,807
It's all I've dreamed about since that awful night I ate you.

348
00:20:52,807 --> 00:20:53,807
Oh, Rhea.

349
00:20:53,807 --> 00:20:56,807
I've been holding on to something precious I need to return to you.

350
00:20:57,807 --> 00:20:59,807
In a box, in the middle of my drawers.

351
00:21:00,807 --> 00:21:02,807
The moon girl and the forest girl.

352
00:21:02,807 --> 00:21:05,807
That box has the rest of your picture book in it.

353
00:21:07,807 --> 00:21:10,807
It was the dream of our love that never materialized.

354
00:21:13,807 --> 00:21:17,807
I couldn't seem to help myself I wanted it so desperately I stole it.

355
00:21:17,807 --> 00:21:19,807
Please forgive me.

356
00:21:28,807 --> 00:21:29,807
Yes, you're right.

357
00:21:30,807 --> 00:21:31,807
That will be their destiny.

358
00:21:32,807 --> 00:21:33,807
Their rightful future.

359
00:21:35,807 --> 00:21:36,807
You know the truth, don't you, Rhea?

360
00:21:37,807 --> 00:21:38,807
You know how I feel.

361
00:21:38,807 --> 00:21:40,807
I think you knew before I did.

362
00:21:41,807 --> 00:21:42,807
And I still do.

363
00:21:43,807 --> 00:21:46,807
And we'll be friends forever, won't we?

364
00:21:48,807 --> 00:21:50,807
Yes, forever and ever.

365
00:21:52,807 --> 00:21:53,807
I love you.

366
00:23:36,999 --> 00:23:43,139
I can't believe Miss Yuriyika was the bear that killed mom.

367
00:23:44,319 --> 00:23:46,139
That will be their destiny.

368
00:23:46,899 --> 00:23:48,339
Their rightful future.

369
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:50,379
Here it is.

370
00:23:50,779 --> 00:23:51,319
The end.

371
00:23:51,579 --> 00:23:52,659
Ginkgo's in my future?

372
00:23:53,479 --> 00:23:54,699
It can't be.

373
00:23:55,219 --> 00:23:56,139
That's impossible.

